From 163545ab36387d81ecfb80331d89003943b63500 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Senior Matthew <SeniorMatt@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 13:38:41 +0500
Subject: [PATCH 04/25] kcm_style: grid filled off the first frame, icon and
 toolbar options on a sub-page
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Page type: Gallery (docs/page-design.md section 5). Config keys (kdeglobals KDE/widgetStyle, unionStyle, icon and
toolbar keys), the GTK D-Bus calls (org.kde.GtkConfig), style plugins and the Breeze settings dialog are unchanged.

Moved / renamed:
- "Configure Icons and Toolbars…" was a popup dialog; now the sub-page "Icons and Toolbars…" (kcm.push), a Form with
  an untitled first section (Show icons: On buttons, In menus) and a "Toolbars" section (main and secondary toolbar
  label). Same four keys (kcm_style/iconsOnButtons, iconsInMenus, toolButtonStyle, toolButtonStyleOtherToolbars).
- "Configure GNOME/GTK Application Style…" -> "GNOME/GTK Application Style…"; its page is a Form page now
  (KCM.SimpleKCM + FormLayout instead of a bare Kirigami.Page with a Flow); the remove button got a text and tooltip
  ("Remove Theme"). "Install From File…" -> "Install from File…".
- Page actions stay top right (Install from File…, Icons and Toolbars…, GNOME/GTK Application Style…); per-style
  Configure Style / Uninstall stay GridDelegate actions. Busy indicator after 150 ms.
- Per ia/duplicates.md nothing is removed: toolbar/icon keys are also synced to GTK by kde-gtk-config.
- Relabel table: inventory/relabel/kcm_style.tsv (outer repo). Inventory --strict: 47 rows ok, 0 lost.

Speed (cause from code, not measured):
- GtkPage::GtkPage() called load(), and KCMStyle::load() called it again: each run scanned every GTK theme
  directory (gtkthemesmodel.cpp:23-31, 125-140) and made a blocking org.kde.GtkConfig.gtkTheme() D-Bus call
  (gtkpage.cpp load(); this call can wait for service activation). isSaveNeeded(), asked on every change, made the
  same blocking call again. Now: no load in the constructor, the call is async, the scan runs one event-loop turn
  later, the selection is applied when both are done (generation counter drops stale loads), and isSaveNeeded()
  compares with the value read at load/save. onThemeRemoved() keeps its order (scan, defaults, save).
- StylesModel::load() (QStyleFactory::keys() plus one KConfig per themerc file) and UnionStylesModel::refresh()
  (Union package scan, was in its constructor) ran before the first frame; now one event-loop turn later
  (KCMStyle::loading property).
- Every card's PreviewItem builds a QStyle plus a QWidget tree in componentComplete() (previewitem.cpp:95-143); the
  thumbnail Loader is now asynchronous, so the cards are created incrementally between frames and show the
  placeholder until ready. Widgets stay on the main thread, so this is spreading, not removing, the cost.
- Numbers: before (build/bench/clean/before-slow.tsv) among the slowest pages. After: pending, manager will measure.

HIG: HIG-001, HIG-005, HIG-006, HIG-019, HIG-047, HIG-058.

Not built yet (freeze).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
